# What a machine thinks of you, read at play zoom, in daylight and at night.
# The wave A build said disposition in one channel only: a blink count on a lamp
# a pixel across, and hostile was the DIMMEST of the four. At noon a hostile
# harvester carried one lit pixel in the whole frame. So: every disposition, at
# the zoom the game is actually played at, at noon and at 23:00, through the real
# mechanisms that set it — a role for the three a machine is born with, and a
# real theft off the plan's own works for the fourth.
#   tools/tour.sh tours/machine-read.tour --seed=1 --weather=clear:0
# The hour and the weather are pinned in the LAST command before every shot, and
# nothing waits after them: the world clock runs while a tour walks, a loaded
# machine turned the night act into the next morning once already, and a keeper
# that keeps its round walked out of frame 02 in the third of a second the frame
# used to wait.
#
# Every machine is staged by a `try` block that clears the ground, spawns and
# then waits on an await only that machine can answer: `machine:KIND` is true
# when a live body of that kind stands far enough inside the frame that the
# shutter will hold it (15_lights.tour_seen). Nothing walks. `spawn` already puts
# a body in view in front of the player, and `walkto mob N` — which steers for at
# most N seconds and then returns true whether or not it arrived — is what made
# the first version of frame 02 come out EMPTY on about half its runs and ship as
# proof of a read nothing in the picture supported.
#
# The WARDEN is why the block retries. It is the roster's only keeper, so it is
# the only body that is wary by role, and a warden put down beside somebody
# arrests them and walks off: measured, it is gone from the frame inside ninety
# frames, every time. No approach could ever have held one. The block spawns a
# fresh one and shoots the moment the await says it is there, and if eight tries
# cannot manage it the tour stops instead of saving the village without it.
#
# It ends on the other half of the same finding: light that does not touch the
# world. A machine's lens was in the glint list alone, which only mirrors in WET
# ground, and the Burning's vents laid nothing on the ground at noon at all.
coast calm
zoom 15
weather clear:0

# --- noon ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# The village square the player wakes in, asked for by name. It used to read
# `at 200.5,431.5`, which is the seed-1 spawn tile to the half-tile and would
# have stopped being it the next time worldgen moved the island. Ten frames
# across four tours were staged on that one number.
hour 12
place spawn
wait 1.2

# indifferent: a worker on its round, nothing of yours.
try 8
	coast calm
	wait 0.35
	spawn harvester
	await machine:harvester 1.2
end
hour 12
weather clear:0
shot 01-noon-indifferent with mob:harvester

# wary: a keeper, which starts one rung up the ladder and keeps its round.
coast calm
wait 0.5
place spawn
try 8
	coast calm
	wait 0.35
	spawn warden
	await machine:warden 1.2
end
hour 12
weather clear:0
shot 02-noon-wary with mob:warden

# observant: a watcher, which never fights and only ever files.
coast calm
wait 0.5
place spawn
try 8
	coast calm
	wait 0.35
	spawn watcher
	await machine:watcher 1.2
end
hour 12
weather clear:0
shot 03-noon-observant with mob:watcher

# hostile: the same kind as frame 01, after the player put their hands on the
# plan's own parts. This is the pillar — rob it and it comes — and it is the
# frame that used to be indistinguishable from 01.
coast calm
near survey
wait 0.6
spawn harvester
wait 1.4
# A survey post has WORDS on it and is also the plan's WORKS (49_story reads it,
# Takes robs it), and one key answers both: the first press reads the readout,
# the second puts it down, and the third gets the hands on the post itself.
press use 0.3
wait 0.3
press use 0.2
wait 0.3
press use 0.3
await theft 8
await turned 4
await machine:harvester 3
hour 12
weather clear:0
shot 04-noon-hostile with mob:harvester

# --- night --------------------------------------------------------------------
# The same four. Whatever the daylight channel gains, the night must not shout.
coast calm
hour 23
weather clear:0
place spawn
wait 1.4

try 8
	coast calm
	wait 0.35
	spawn harvester
	await machine:harvester 1.2
end
hour 23
weather clear:0
shot 05-night-indifferent with mob:harvester

coast calm
wait 0.5
place spawn
try 8
	coast calm
	wait 0.35
	spawn warden
	await machine:warden 1.2
end
hour 23
weather clear:0
shot 06-night-wary with mob:warden

coast calm
wait 0.5
place spawn
try 8
	coast calm
	wait 0.35
	spawn watcher
	await machine:watcher 1.2
end
hour 23
weather clear:0
shot 07-night-observant with mob:watcher

coast calm
near survey
wait 0.6
spawn harvester
wait 1.4
# The same three presses the noon frame above needs, and for the same reason: the
# post is read, put down, and only then robbed. One press here read the words and
# stole nothing, so nothing turned — and `await theft` passed anyway, because
# 32_disposition remembers a theft for the life of the run (see the night frame's
# own note in docs/ROADMAP.md). The frame is of a machine that has turned, so it
# has to actually turn one.
press use 0.3
wait 0.3
press use 0.2
wait 0.3
press use 0.3
await theft 8
await turned 4
await machine:harvester 3
hour 23
weather clear:0
shot 08-night-hostile with mob:harvester

# --- machine light lands on the ground -----------------------------------------
# A watcher at night threw nothing on the ground it stood on: its lens was in the
# glint list, which only mirrors in WET ground. Close, so the pool round its feet
# is a thing a player can see, and on the machines' power so it stutters.
# Open ground by name; tours/machines-day.tour says what it replaced.
coast calm
hour 23
weather clear:0
place open_coast
zoom 15
wait 1.4
try 8
	coast calm
	wait 0.35
	spawn watcher
	await machine:watcher 1.2
end
# Close, and only then in: a body is put down in view at the zoom it was put
# down at, and eight units of view is narrower than the arm's length it lands at.
# A watcher does not move (pace 0.1), so walking up to one is not a chase.
walkto mob 1.6
zoom 8
await machine:watcher 3
hour 23
weather clear:0
shot 09-its-light-on-the-ground with mob:watcher

# --- the land's own fire lands on the land ---------------------------------------
# The other half of the same finding: at noon the Burning was white-hot cores
# sitting on flat ground with nothing under them. A lamp lit at noon still lays
# nothing — but a vent is a hole into fire, and it reaches the ground it is in at
# every hour. Both hours, so the night it already had is visibly the night it keeps.
coast calm
place burning
near vent
zoom 8
hour 12
weather clear:0
wait 1.2
shot 10-a-vent-at-noon
hour 23
weather clear:0
wait 1.2
shot 11-the-same-vent-at-night
